      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>The destination delivery handover for two‑wheelers and motorcycles is a structured process that ensures the vehicle’s condition is verified, documented, and formally accepted by both the carrier and the consignee. The procedure is performed during daylight to allow clear visual assessment and to compare the current state of the vehicle with the original pickup documentation.</p>
<p>This step‑by‑step guide outlines the three critical checkpoints: daylight re‑inspection against pickup photos, odometer verification against the LR (Waybill) bilty, and the final signed condition sign‑off.</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
